From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:38:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] uml: answer the mconsole "mem" command with the memory
 counters

Andarium shows how much memory the guest itself uses, and the host
cannot get it from a file. The management console's "proc meminfo"
opens /proc/meminfo, which an Android guest's SELinux policy denies
the console, and it needs a process context to do so.

Add "mem", which replies with the three counters /proc/meminfo calls
MemTotal, MemAvailable and MemFree, in bytes:

    total=<n> available=<n> free=<n>

The reply is one datagram of decimal numbers, a single space between
the fields and nothing after them. The command reads si_meminfo() and
si_mem_available(), neither of which sleeps or opens a file, so it is
answered from the console's interrupt, like "stack" and "go". A kernel
without the command answers "Unknown command" with the error flag, and
nothing else about it changes.
---
 arch/um/drivers/mconsole.h      |  1 +
 arch/um/drivers/mconsole_kern.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/um/drivers/mconsole_user.c |  1 +
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/mconsole.h b/arch/um/drivers/mconsole.h
index c7f19b031a125fd7d8ab4d022559350f1c45cbac..e536d3afedf1cb73b2cb97186f87775e5cb0b479 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/mconsole.h
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/mconsole.h
@@ -89,6 +89,7 @@ extern void mconsole_wake(struct mc_request *req);
 extern void mconsole_log(struct mc_request *req);
 extern void mconsole_proc(struct mc_request *req);
 extern void mconsole_stack(struct mc_request *req);
+extern void mconsole_mem(struct mc_request *req);
 extern void mconsole_trim(struct mc_request *req);
 
 extern int mconsole_get_request(int fd, struct mc_request *req);
diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_kern.c b/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_kern.c
index 5fc5a60835ab307a691943899b6c53893ab2762d..6ff80357a47ff93f6459f0a4515610e695d59f7a 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_kern.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_kern.c
@@ -126,6 +126,25 @@ void mconsole_log(struct mc_request *req)
 	mconsole_reply(req, "", 0, 0);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The figures /proc/meminfo calls MemTotal, MemAvailable and MemFree, in
+ * bytes.  They come straight from the page counters, so the reply needs
+ * neither a file nor a process context, and a guest whose policy keeps
+ * the console out of /proc/meminfo answers all the same.
+ */
+void mconsole_mem(struct mc_request *req)
+{
+	struct sysinfo info;
+	char reply[96];
+
+	si_meminfo(&info);
+	snprintf(reply, sizeof(reply), "total=%llu available=%llu free=%llu",
+		 (u64) info.totalram * info.mem_unit,
+		 (u64) si_mem_available() << PAGE_SHIFT,
+		 (u64) info.freeram * info.mem_unit);
+	mconsole_reply(req, reply, 0, 0);
+}
+
 void mconsole_proc(struct mc_request *req)
 {
 	struct vfsmount *mnt = proc_mnt;
@@ -196,6 +215,7 @@ void mconsole_proc(struct mc_request *req)
     log <string> - make UML enter <string> into the kernel log\n\
     proc <file> - returns the contents of the UML's /proc/<file>\n\
     stack <pid> - returns the stack of the specified pid\n\
+    mem - returns the memory total=, available= and free=, in bytes\n\
     trim on|off|once - trim page cache the host already caches:\n\
 	periodically, no longer, or all of the cold cache now\n\
 "
diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_user.c b/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_user.c
index 27c38f2f26f4ba841d48b565ba754744a5c2be2c..6ead5ac46da71436c324b8579e0b853d52964616 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_user.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/mconsole_user.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ static struct mconsole_command commands[] = {
 	{ "log", mconsole_log, MCONSOLE_INTR },
 	{ "proc", mconsole_proc, MCONSOLE_PROC },
 	{ "stack", mconsole_stack, MCONSOLE_INTR },
+	{ "mem", mconsole_mem, MCONSOLE_INTR },
 	{ "trim", mconsole_trim, MCONSOLE_PROC },
 };
 
